red when establishing a ± 1% error bound under the conditions listed above.\n9.  A BICUBICINTERPOLATION function in EXCEL is required to read the two look-up tables, and the file must be macro-enabled (it is .xlsm).  I use EXCEL 2016. \n10. LRCINOP and HOLDINGINOP use Boeing tabulated Machs and fuel flows.\n11. HOLDING and HOLDINGINOP fuel flows are for straight flight with no turns (i.e., the 5% turns penalty has been removed from the Boeing tables).  The turns penalty may be added  when using the Endurance Model worksheet.\n","formula":null,"match":"value"}
