RANGE Fuel Flow Model!A1:N90
{"kind":"table","sheet":"Fuel Flow Model","address":"A1:N90","rows":90,"cols":14,"values":[[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"9M-MRO Fuel Model - Dr. Bobby Ulich",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.0 Beta",43003,"(1) Initial issue.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.1 Beta",43009,"(1) Added Mach and Fuel Flow tables for Maximum Range Cruise (Cost Index = 0) and for Cost Index = 52 (MH370 Flight Plan); (2) Added capability to select a standard speed mode (MRC, LRC, CI=52, M0.84, or Holding) or an arbitrary Mach; (3) Added switch to select Air Packs ON or Air Packs OFF (OFF saves ≈55 kg/hr/engine).  Estimated RMS Mach errors are 0.8% for CI = 52 and 1.1% for MRC.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.2 Beta",43010,"(1) Added Endurance Model worksheet.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.3 Beta",43019,"(1) Added constant KCAS speed mode; (2) Modified Endurance Model  to find L and R engine flame-out times; (3) Added numerous input parameters to Endurance Model, allowing for 3 legs, climbs, descents, etc.; (4) Added end-of-flight model.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.4",43030,"(1) Added LRCINOP and HOLDINGINOP speed modes; (2) Modified L and R tank calculations in the Endurance Model to allow extended INOP flight using all fuel on board.; (3) Fixed a bug in setting ΔSAT for the 3 legs in the Endurance Model; (4) Added a worksheet with a plot of endurance versus range for various post-18:29 speed modes and altitudes; (5) Revised the CI = 52 Mach schedule.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.5",43043,"(1) Added examples for fixed Mach and fixed KIAS in \"Endurance vs Range Plot\" worksheet.  Also added the southern latitude limits to the table on the same worksheet.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Version 5.6",43043,"(1) Corrected two fuel flow values in the tables.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Notes :\n1. This is a Beta test version.  Please identify possible errors and suggest methods for improvements.  Respond to bobby.ulich@gmail.com.\n2. This is a traditional, generalized aerodynamic model that computes fuel flow as a function of Mach, weight, flight level, temperature deviation from ISA, and average engine PDA.  It assumes level flight at constant air speed.\n3. This model is only applicable to a B777-200ER aircraft with Rolls Royce Trent 892B engines (like 9M-MRO).\n4. The truth data used to fit this model are the accompanying tables of fuel flow prepared by Boeing.  See the other worksheets for a complete listing of all applicable speed and fuel flow tables.\n5. Generally speaking, applicable weights are those above 170 tonnes, and flight levels are between 200-430 for full accuracy (within ± 1%).  LRC data are used down to FL100, and somewhat degraded accuracy is expected below FL200 at low speeds (estimated ± 2%).\n6.  The Holding fuel flow tables exhibit \"steps\" of 1%, 2.5%, and 5% which are not fully understood.  The steps > 1% in fuel flow produce \"outliers\" which have been removed from the data set being fitted.\n7. The  airfoil drag coefficients are accessed using a 2-D look-up table, which is based on Obert's plot with very minor (<1%) adjustments to best fit the truth data.\n8. The engine effectiveness in producing thrust appears to depend on the ratio of thrust to the static air pressure (in addition to depending on Mach and static air temperature).  An empirical fit to this function is used in the Thrust Specific Fuel Consumption parameter.  See the Figures worksheet for a plot.  The thrust to pressure ratio  is correlated with the drag curves, so it is possible that the small (< 1%) variations seen in the best-fit TSFC effectiveness parameter are actually due to inaccuracies in interpolating the drag coefficient, not to engine characteristics.  This effect is considered when establishing a ± 1% error bound under the conditions listed above.\n9.  A BICUBICINTERPOLATION function in EXCEL is required to read the two look-up tables, and the file must be macro-enabled (it is .xlsm).  I use EXCEL 2016. \n10. LRCINOP and HOLDINGINOP use Boeing tabulated Machs and fuel flows.\n11. HOLDING and HOLDINGINOP fuel flows are for straight flight with no turns (i.e., the 5% turns penalty has been removed from the Boeing tables).  The turns penalty may be added  when using the Endurance Model worksheet.\n",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Parameters","Values","Units","Notes","Equations",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Inputs :",null,null,null,"Line #",null,"FF2used (kg/hr)",null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Speed_Mode","LRCINOP","(--)","Select one: MACH, KCAS, LRC, MRC, CI52, M0.84, HOLDING, LRCINOP, HOLDINGINOP",6,"Manual entry of Speed_Mode","#NAME?",null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Fixed Mach or KCAS",0.821,"(--)","Manually-entered Mach used when Speed_Mode is set to MACH, or manually-entered KCAS when Speed_Mode is set to KCAS",14,"Manual entry of Mach or KCAS",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Weight",210,"(tonnes)","Total weight W of aircraft including Fuel on Board",15,"Manual entry of weight",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Flight Level",350,"(hft)","Pressure altitude in units of 100 feet",16,"Manual entry of flight level",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"ΔSAT (C)",10,"(C)","Difference between Static Air Temperature (SAT) and International Standard Atmosphere (ISA) temperature at same pressure altitude; affects true airspeed and fuel flow",17,"Manual entry of temperature deviation from ISA",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Air Conditioning Packs","ON","(ON or OFF)","Normally ON; turning Air Packs OFF reduces fuel flow by approx. 88 kg/hr/engine and depressurizes cabin",18,"Manual entry of \"ON\" or \"OFF\" for air packs",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"PDA",0.015,"(%)","Engine Performance Degradation Allowance; average of left and right engine values for 9M-MRO is 1.5% from MH370 Flight Plan",19,"Manual entry of PDA in %",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Outputs :",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Mach","#NAME?","(--)","Selects or calculates Mach from Speed_Mode and fixed input; Mach number M is ratio of true airspeed to Local Sound Speed",21,"=IF(G7=\"MACH\",G8, IF(G7=\"KCAS\",  ( (5*( (   (((1+0.2*(G8/661.4786)^2)^3.5 -1)  )/( (1-6.8755856*10^-6 *100*G10)^5.2558797) +1)^(2/7) -1) )^0.5),IF(G7=\"LRC\",BicubicInterpolation( 'LRC Mach'!$C$4:$AL$21, G10,G9),  IF(G7=\"MRC\",BicubicInterpolation( 'MRC Mach'!$C$3:$T$18, G10,G9),  IF(G7=\"M0.84\",0.84,  IF(G7=\"CI52\",BicubicInterpolation('CI=52 Mach'!$C$3:$T$18, G10,G9),  IF(G7=\"HOLDING\",BicubicInterpolation(  'Holding Mach'!$C$4:$M$13, G10,G9),\nIF(G7=\"LRCINOP\", BicubicInterpolation('LRC INOP Mach'!$C$4:$AA$21,G10,G9), IF(G7=\"HOLDINGINOP\",  BicubicInterpolation('Holding INOP Mach'!$N$4:$U$13,G10,G9),\"TRY AGAIN\" )))))))))",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"SATISA",218.80799999999996,"(K)","ISA Static Air Temperature at Flight Level",22,"=IF(G10<360.8924,288.15-1.9812*G10/10,216.65)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"θISA",0.759354502863092,null,"Ratio of SATISA at Flight Level to SATISA at sea level (288.15 K)",23,"=G16/288.15",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"SAT",228.80799999999996,"(K)","Static Air Temperature, including ΔSAT",24,"=G16+G11",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"θ",0.7940586500086759,"(--)","Ratio of SAT at Flight Level to SATISA at sea level (288.15 K)",25,"=G18/288.15",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"TAT","#NAME?","(K)","Total Air Temperature including dynamic heating = SAT·(1+0.2·M2)",26,"=G18*(1+0.2*G15^2)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"θT","#NAME?","(--)","Ratio of Total Air Temperature (TAT) to SATISA at sea level (288.15 K)",27,"=G20/288.15",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"(θT)0.68","#NAME?","(--)","Power of θT used in corrected fuel flow parameter is best fit to Boeing 777-200ER LRC and Holding fuel flow tables for RR Trent 892B engines; note that this term adjusts fuel flow with temperature (no additional temperature correction factor, such as 3%/10C in TAT, is needed)",28,"=G21^0.68",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"LSS",589.4433726144483,"(kts)","Local Sound Speed",29,"=661.4786*SQRT(G19)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"TAS","#NAME?","(kts)","True airspeed",30,"=G15*G23",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,"#NAME?","(m/s)",null,31,"=G24*0.5144444",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"KCAS","#NAME?","(kts)","Knots Calibrated Air Speed",32,"=661.4786*(5*((1 + ( (1-0.00068755856*G10)^5.2558797)*((1 + G15^2/5)^3.5 - 1))^(2/7) - 1))^0.5",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"P",238.42273848320244,"(hPa)","Static atmospheric pressure at given Flight Level (pressure altitude)",33,"=IF(G10<360.8924,1013.25*(1-0.0000068755856*100*G10)^5.2558797,0.01*0.2233609*101325*EXP(-0.004806346*(G10-360.8924)))",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"δ",0.23530494792321976,"(--)","Ratio of static air pressure at Flight Level to ISA sea-level pressure (1013.25 hPa)",34,"=G27/1013.25",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"δT","#NAME?","(--)","Total pressure ratio is ratio of dynamic air pressure to static sea-level air pressure; dynamic pressure is P·(1+0.2·M2)3.5",35,"=G28*(1+0.2*G15^2)^3.5",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"W0  ≡  W / δ",892.4589212995352,"(tonnes)","Ratio of aircraft total weight to pressure ratio δ; equals weight at sea level having same ratio to sea-level pressure as actual weight to actual pressure at given Flight Level",36,"=G9/G28",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"ρ",0.36300663836707125,"(kg/m3)","Air density =1.225·δ / θ",37,"=1.225*G28/G19",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"S",427.8,"(m2)","Reference wing area of B777-200ER; design value is 427.80 m2",38,427.8,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"CL","#NAME?","(--)","Coefficient of lift calculated assuming lift = weight (i.e., no vertical acceleration)",39,"=1000*9.80665*G9/(0.5*G31*G32*(G25)^2)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"CD","#NAME?","(--)","Drag coefficient is calculated using bicubic interpolation of lookup table for B777-200ER",40,"=0.0001*BicubicInterpolation('Drag Coef Table'!$B$4:$L$28,G33,G15)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"ΔCD",0.00011693948899576943,"(--)","Correction to drag coefficient due to Reynolds number; here this correction is only for temperature; correction for effect of pressure on Reynolds number depends on Boeing reference altitude chart, which is unpublished in open literature; +10C increases drag and fuel flow by ≈ 0.5%",41,"=(-45.29)*0.0001*LOG10(  (  ( G19 + 0.38312 ) / G19^2    )   /   (   (G17 +0.38312)/(G17)^2  ) )",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"CDtotal","#NAME?","(--)","Total drag coefficient, including effect of temperature on Reynolds number",42,"=G34+G35",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"L / D = CL / CDtotal","#NAME?","(--)","Ratio of lift to drag = ratio of lift coefficient to drag coefficient",43,"=G33/G36",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Thrust ≡ Ͳ = Drag ≡ D","#NAME?","(kN)","Required thrust equals drag, assuming constant airspeed",44,"=G36*0.5*G31*(G25^2)*G32/1000",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Drag/δ ≡ D0 = Ͳ/δ ≡ Ͳ0","#NAME?","tonnes","For this ratio I use tonnes rather than kN for thrust, to be consistent with the standard practice of listing aircraft weights in tonnes (1,000 kg)",45,"=G38/G28/9.80665",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"TSFC_Scalar",75.1967,"(kg/hr/kN/1 engine)","Best-fit coefficient of TSFC (at sea level at Mach 1) for Rolls Royce Trent 892B engines",46,75.1967,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"θ0.68",0.8548693671408469,"(--)","Temperature dependence factor in TSFC",47,"=G19^0.68",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"M0.53","#NAME?","(--)","Mach dependence factor in TSFC",48,"=G15^0.53",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Eeng","#NAME?","(--)","The engine effectiveness factor in TSFC, depending on the ratio of thrust to static air pressure (Ͳ0) from a best-fit look-up table; Eeng ≤ 1",49,"=BicubicInterpolation('TSFC Eff Table'!$B$4:$E$69,2,G39)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"TSFC","#NAME?","(kg/hr/kN)","Thrust-specific fuel consumption for RR Trent 892B engines = TSFC_Scalar · θ0.68 · M0.5 /  Eeng ",50,"=G40*G41*G42/G43",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FFnet2new","#NAME?","(kg/hr/2 new engines)","Thrust-producing (net) fuel flow from two new engines = Thrust · TSFC",51,"=IF( G7=\"LRCINOP\",   BicubicInterpolation('LRC INOP FF'!$C$4:$AA$21,G10,G9)-G50,  IF(G7=\"HOLDINGINOP\",   BicubicInterpolation( 'Holding INOP FF'!$C$4:$J$13, G10,  G9)/1.05-G50, G38*G44))",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FFnet1new","#NAME?","(kg/hr/1 new engine)","Single-engine net fuel flow that produces thrust (with new engines)",52,"=IF( OR(G7=\"LRCINOP\", G7=\"HOLDINGINOP\"),  G45, G45/2  )",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"CFFnet1new","#NAME?","(tonnes/hr/1 new engine)","Corrected fuel flow parameter using thrust-producing fuel flow for 1 new engine \n= FFnet1new/(δT · θT0.68)",53,"=G46/(G29*G22)/1000",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"CFFnet2new","#NAME?","(tonnes/hr/2 new engines)","Corrected fuel flow parameter using thrust-producing fuel flow for 2 new engines",54,"=IF( OR(G7=\"LRCINOP\", G7=\"HOLDINGINOP\"), G47,  2*G47 )",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"CFFnet2new / W0","#NAME?","(%/hr)","Ratio of Corrected (net) Fuel Flow parameter for 2 new engines to equivalent sea-level weight W0; assumes new engines (PDA = 0%); typically ≈ 2% of equivalent aircraft weight is burned per hour at unity dynamic pressure and temperature ratios",55,"=100*G48/G30",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FF0",200,"(kg/hr/1 new engine)","Non-thrust-producing fuel flow (i.e., ancillary/parasitic fuel flow, or fuel flow at zero thrust) in 1 new engine; supplies bleed air, drives integrated electrical generators, hydraulic pump and fuel pump, and includes parasitic engine losses; value is best fit to Boeing fuel flow tables for this aircraft and engine type; is a primary component of idle engine fuel flow; =200 kg/hr/engine with Air Conditioning Packs ON and ≈145 kg/hr/engine with Air Packs OFF; estimate of Air Packs is 2.5% of typical cruise fuel flow of 3500 kg/hr/engine = 88 kg/hr/engine",56,"=200-IF(G12'=\"OFF\",88,0)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FF1new","#NAME?","(kg/hr/1 new engine)","Total fuel flow for 1 new engine, including non-thrust-producing fuel flow",57,"=G46+G50",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FF2new = 2 ·FF1new","#NAME?","(kg/hr/2 new engines)","Total fuel flow for 2 new engines, including non-thrust-producing fuel flow",58,"=IF( OR(G7=\"LRCINOP\", G7=\"HOLDINGINOP\"), G51, 2*G51 )",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FMnew","#NAME?","(NM/tonne)","Fuel mileage for new engines",59,"=1000*G24/G52",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FF1used","#NAME?","(kg/hr/1 used engine)","Total fuel flow for 1 used engines (increased by PDA)",60,"=G51*(1+G13)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FF2used","#NAME?","(kg/hr/2 used engines)","Total fuel flow for 2 used engines (increased by PDA)",61,"=G52*(1+G13)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"FMused","#NAME?","(NM/tonne)","Fuel mileage for 2 used engines",62,"=1000*G24/G55",null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null